    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="Inscr.">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:VIAtr">VI Atr</ref> Inscr.</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="VI Atr. Inscr.">[Not in D]</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-k">Be witena gerædnessan</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-k">Concerning the ordinances of the councillors.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Von Beschlüssen der Witan.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">Of the decisions of the witan.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="246"><ref target="clause:VAtr_Inscr">V Atr Inscr.</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. V[?] Ins[cr.]</note>
        <note type="comparisonIncomplete">Some of Liebermann’s notes here are cut off in the gutter of the scan used, and are still to be completed.</note>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann's base text for 1–15.1 is K (Cotton Claudius A III f. 31v, mid-11th c., after the Latin paraphrase); D (CCCC 201) begins only at 16. ‘K.’ (capitul) stands before each chapter in K. Dated 16 May 1008–13 May 1011. Perhaps VI Atr derives from the same law as V Atr (Liebermann).</note>
      </div>
